{"qid": "76265631", "kind": "insufficient_context", "language": "python", "title": "ChromaDb add single document, only if it doesn't exist", "answer": "You can use the `add_document` method of the `Chroma` class to add a single document to the database. This method takes a document and returns a boolean indicating whether the document was added successfully. You can use this method in a loop to check if the document exists before adding it.\n\nHere is an example of how you can do this:\n\n```python\nfrom langchain.vectorstores import Chroma\n\n# Initialize the Chroma database\ndb = Chroma.from_documents([], embeddings, persist_directory='db')\n\n# Define the document you want to add\ndocument = {'text': 'This is a test document'}\n\n# Check if the document exists\nif not db.add_document(document):\n    # If the document does not exist, get embeddings and add it\n    embeddings = OpenAIEmbeddings()\n    db.add_document(document, embeddings)\n    print(f'Added document: {document}')\nelse:\n    print(f'Document already exists: {document}')\n```", "valid_output": true, "insufficient_information": false, "retrieved": ["llama_index/docs/docs/understanding/storing/storing.md_0_4924", "langchain/docs/docs/how_to/indexing.ipynb_0_7842", "langchain/docs/docs/how_to/vectorstores.mdx_0_5549", "langchain/libs/partners/chroma/langchain_chroma/vectorstores.py_4107_13535", "langchainjs/docs/core_docs/docs/integrations/vectorstores/chroma.ipynb_0_6875", "langchain/docs/docs/integrations/vectorstores/chroma.ipynb_0_6483", "langchain/libs/community/langchain_community/vectorstores/chroma.py_0_9468", "chroma/docs/docs.trychroma.com/pages/reference/cheatsheet.md_0_6165"], "n_candidates": 62, "cited_doc_ids": ["langchain/docs/docs/how_to/indexing.ipynb_0_7842", "langchain/docs/docs/how_to/vectorstores.mdx_0_5549", "langchain/libs/partners/chroma/langchain_chroma/vectorstores.py_4107_13535", "langchainjs/docs/core_docs/docs/integrations/vectorstores/chroma.ipynb_0_6875", "langchain/libs/